{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5303: implement srd030-md5sum R3.1-R3.3 requirements for the `cmd/md5sum` utility in the go-unix-utils project. This is a \"stitch\" task in a code generation pipeline. The specific requirements are:\n   - R3.1: `-b` (`--binary`) marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\" format (one space + asterisk). On Linux/macOS there is no functional difference in digest computation.\n   - R3.2: `-t` (`--text`) is the default; output uses \"HASH  FILENAME\" (two spaces).\n   - R3.3: When `--tag` is given with `-b`, output is BSD tag format; the mode flag has no effect on tag format.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/md5sum/main.go` and `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go`.\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: All R3.1-R3.3 implemented, differential tests pass against `gmd5sum`, `go build` succeeds, `go test` passes, `go vet` clean.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gmd5sum`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `pkg/hashutil` package provides `FormatGNU`, `FormatBSDTag`, `DigestFiles`, `VerifyChecksums`, `ComputeDigest`, `ParseChecksumLine`\n   - `hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, binary, tag, stdout, stderr)` handles output formatting\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - GNU format: \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: \"MD5 (FILENAME) = HASH\"\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct with Name, Args, Stdin, ExitCode, Normalize fields\n   - LC_ALL=C required for all differential tests\n   - No git commands allowed; orchestrator manages git externally\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/spe